   "about": "A prefecture-wide roster records the locations, founding dates, enrollments, and teaching staffs of public and private educational institutions in Fukushima Prefecture.",
   "summary": "The document continues a long roster with the final entries for village- and town-controlled youth schools and then lists 483 coeducational elementary schools, followed by municipal kindergartens. It subsequently catalogs private commercial, middle, youth, elementary, kindergarten, and miscellaneous special schools. Most tables compare recorded enrollment and teacher numbers on 30 April and 30 November 1946, distinguish male and female enrollment, and identify full- and part-time teachers; notes also identify branch schools and institutions closed during 1946.",
